Chief: Have you heard what's going on out there?

Harlow: No doubt some sort of monkey trouble and I'm the man to fix it.

Boffin: Giant apes are attacking the city!

Harlow: ...

Chief: Normally we'd bring in the national guard. But even in emergencies we have to go by the book...

Boffin: Article 1, Section 4, Clause 17: The newly incorporated Federal monkey patrol is given full reponsibility to deal with all monkey related problems within city limits; including but not limited to: catching circus escapees, peeling bananas during official functions and cleaning up after code browns. The city will supply the department with buckets, mops and other equipment to carry out these duties.

Chief: You can see why you're here. Some bureacrat put you in charge of monkeys and so formalities require your signature to bring in the army. Here, sign here. And here.

Harlow: This is my departments juristiction? I think I can handle it. Of course... to fix this I'm going to need my pilot's licence back.

Chief: You can't be serious! Harlow these are giant monkeys and they're destroying the city! The army must be brought in! Imagine how it would look on my record! People could die!

Mayor: Good day, gentlemen.
